{"resourceIdentifier":"4015","resourceName":"Sanergy Composting Group Project","description":"The Sanergy Composting Group Project is located in Kenya and produces compost and compressed fuel briquettes from various organic and biomass waste sources. These waste sources include food waste, wood dust, sugarcane bagasse, slaughterhouse waste and human sanitation waste. The processes also entail a pre-treatment step with the use of black soldier fly (BSF) insect larvae, which valorize some of the organics in an aerobic process and leave behind a residue which is called frass. The frass is then mixed with other types of organic waste aerobically composted into organic fertilizer for local farmers. Furthermore, the frass can be mixed and compressed into biomass briquettes which are in part used on site, and the residual briquettes are sold to local industry as a renewable fuel for industrial boilers generating heat and steam. \r\n\r\nThe first project activity instance is located in Nairobi, Kenya. Sanergy Limited is the owner of the facility located in Nairobi and is the Project Developer for the Sanergy Composting Group Project. Circular Impact is the project proponent.","location":{"latitude":-1.347790,"longitude":37.054990},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-01-12","endExclusive":"2023-02-12","endInclusive":"2023-02-11"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4015"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Circular Impact, Inc."},{"type":"string","value":"ON, Canada"},{"type":"string","value":"+254 115611760"},{"type":"string","value":"haroon@circularimpact.io"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"4015"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"33658"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY